  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "What is the dimension of ${R}_{2}[t]$, the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $2?$",
  "worked_solution": "The standard basis of ${R}_{n}[t]$ is\n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,\u2026,\\,{t}^{n}}.\n$$\n\nSo, the standard basis of ${R}_{2}[t]$ is \n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{2}[t])=3.\n$$\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{n}[t])=n+1.\n$$",
